# The build context for proxy/Dockerfile is the repository root, so without this
# every `docker build` uploaded the whole working tree to the daemon: .env (the
# database password), backups/, .git/ and the licensed source PDF (#63).
#
# An ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist: exclude everything, then admit the paths the
# Dockerfile COPYs. A blocklist protects against the secrets someone thought of;
# this protects against the next file nobody did. If proxy/Dockerfile needs
# another path, add it here, and tests/test_dockerignore.py will tell you if
# that opens something it should not.
*
!proxy/Caddyfile
!proxy/csp.caddy
!docs/app/
